# .railwayignore — gitignore-style filter for `railway up` (and the watch trigger).
#
# Why this file exists: this worktree is ~942 MB at the root (the SPA build
# artefacts under operator/ alone are 754 MB), which silently exceeds Railway's
# upload size cap. A `railway up` from the worktree root then "fails before
# build" with no associated build (the upload itself is rejected) instead of
# producing a usable build log.
#
# The jinn-indexer service's Dockerfile build context is `packages/`
# (Root Directory = /packages, dockerfilePath = indexer/deploy/Dockerfile).
# So only `packages/indexer/` and `packages/sdk/` are actually needed for the
# build. Everything else can — and should — be excluded from the upload.
#
# This file is at the REPO ROOT (per Railway's monorepo docs the .railwayignore
# is repo-root-anchored, matching watchPatterns in railway.toml). The
# packages/indexer service's railway.toml lives under packages/indexer/deploy/
# and is unaffected by this filter — Railway reads it via "Config as code".

# ── Exclude everything by default ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── Then re-include only what the indexer Docker build needs ──────────────────
!packages/
packages/*
!packages/indexer/
!packages/indexer/**
!packages/sdk/
!packages/sdk/**

# Inside the included packages, still skip heavy junk that doesn't belong in
# the build context (node_modules, dist outputs, local caches, OS noise).
packages/indexer/node_modules
packages/indexer/.pnp.*
packages/indexer/.yarn/cache
packages/indexer/.yarn/install-state.gz
packages/indexer/.yarn/unplugged
packages/indexer/.ponder
packages/indexer/explorer/node_modules
packages/indexer/explorer/dist
packages/indexer/explorer/.next
packages/sdk/node_modules
packages/sdk/dist
packages/sdk/.yarn/cache
packages/sdk/.yarn/install-state.gz
packages/sdk/.yarn/unplugged

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
*.log
.cursor
.codex
